# Keeps the build context down to the files the image actually serves. The COPYs in
# the Dockerfile name those paths explicitly, so nothing here is load-bearing for the
# image contents — the point is not shipping the rest of the repo to the daemon, and
# making a future `COPY . .` not silently drag tools/ and the git history into an HTTP
# root.

# Version control and this file's own history: the checkout is not the artifact.
.git
.gitignore

# CI runs from the checkout, not from the image.
.github

# The Node suites and the headless-browser checks. Nothing at runtime reads them, and
# inside the image they would sit in the served document root, downloadable at the
# same URLs as the game.
tools/

# Repo documentation, not site content.
README.md

# This file and the compose file are inputs to the build, not outputs of it.
docker-compose.yml

# The Phase 1 server's local state and its test suite. Both builds ignore these: the static
# site has no use for them, and the server image is built from this same context
# (`docker build -f server/Dockerfile .`), where a local database must not be uploaded to
# the daemon — it is one `COPY . .` away from being baked into an image. server/ itself is
# NOT ignored here, because that build needs server/index.js and server/lib/.
server/data
server/test

# macOS noise.
.DS_Store
